# Deterministic incident-correlation policy.
# These values are intentionally conservative defaults and should be tuned
# against real historical incidents after the baseline dataset is built.
rules:
  - id: SAP_LOCK_CONTENTION
    enabled: true
    title: SAP application / lock contention
    severity: CRITICAL
    description: Elevated SAP locks and dialog response time indicate likely application contention.
    confidence: 0.87
    thresholds:
      lock_count: 10
      response_time_ms: 500
      dump_count: 0

    culprit:
      component: SAP application / ABAP
      statement: >-
        A long-running or uncommitted transaction is holding enqueue locks
        while other dialog work waits behind it. The lock holder is named in
        the evidence below -- that user or job is the proximate cause, not the
        host, not the database.
      confirm_in:
        - "SM12 -- identify the oldest lock and its owner"
        - "SM50 -- find that user's work process and its running report"
        - "SM66 -- check whether the same report is running on other instances"
    remediation:
      - "Identify the oldest enqueue entry in SM12 and its holder."
      - "Confirm in SM50/SM66 whether the holder is still active or orphaned."
      - "If orphaned (no matching work process), delete the lock entry in SM12."
      - "If active, contact the owner before cancelling -- deleting a lock under a running update corrupts data."
      - "Recurring on the same object: the ABAP needs a shorter lock scope, not a bigger server."
  - id: INFRA_RESOURCE_PRESSURE
    enabled: true
    title: Infrastructure resource pressure
    severity: CRITICAL
    description: Multiple host resource indicators are saturated or are driving severe response-time degradation.
    confidence: 0.86
    thresholds:
      cpu_percent: 90
      memory_percent: 90
      load_1m: 8
      response_time_ms: 1000
      minimum_high_resources: 2

    culprit:
      component: Host / infrastructure
      statement: >-
        The application server is short of a host resource, so requests queue
        before they reach ABAP. This is a capacity or sizing fault: the SAP
        work is a victim of it, not the cause.
      confirm_in:
        - "ST06 -- physical memory, free memory, Page In/Out of RAM"
        - "ST02 -- extended memory and buffer swaps"
        - "SM50 -- whether work processes are in PRIV mode (heap exhaustion)"
      confirm_notes: >-
        Free memory near zero with Page Out at 0 is ALLOCATED, not exhausted.
        Sustained Page Out above 0 %/h is the signal that matters.
    remediation:
      - "ST06: check Page Out of RAM. Zero means allocated, not exhausted -- do not escalate on free memory alone."
      - "ST02: any non-zero swap count on program/CUA/screen buffers means the buffer is too small."
      - "SM50: work processes in PRIV mode indicate heap exhaustion -- review ztta/roll_extension and abap/heap_area_dia."
      - "Compare em/initial_size_MB and PHYS_MEMSIZE against the real physical memory in ST06."
      - "If CPU-bound: identify the top consumer in ST03N before adding cores."
  - id: SAP_PROCESS_FAILURE
    enabled: true
    title: SAP application server process failure
    severity: CRITICAL
    description: One or more SAP work processes are reporting a critical state.
    confidence: 0.96

    culprit:
      component: SAP work process / dispatcher
      statement: >-
        One or more work processes are in a failed or stopped state. Until
        they are restored, capacity is reduced regardless of host headroom,
        and queueing will look like a performance problem.
      confirm_in:
        - "SM50 -- work process status and any error text"
        - "SM21 -- system log around the failure timestamp"
        - "ST22 -- dumps raised by the affected process"
        - "dev_w<n> trace files in the instance work directory"
    remediation:
      - "SM50: note the failed process number, type and its last report."
      - "SM21: read the system log for the same minute -- the cause is usually logged there."
      - "ST22: check for a dump raised by that process."
      - "Restart the individual work process in SM50 before considering an instance restart."
      - "Repeated failure of the same WP type points at a specific report or an exhausted resource, not at SAP generally."